The graph models an exchange between Australian dollars $d$ and British pounds $p$ on one day.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.5cm,y=0.75cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{conversionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=1,gridGrey,very thin] (0,0) grid (10,6);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(10.7,0) node[right] {$d$ (AUD)};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,6.7) node[above] {$p$ (GBP)};
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8,10}{\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.08);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {1,2,3,4,5,6}{\draw[black] (0,\y)--(-0.12,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\y) {$\y$};}
\draw[thick,conversionBlue] (0,0)--(10,6);
\fill[black] (5,3) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (5,3) {$P$};
\fill[black] (10,6) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (10,6) {$Q$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) Use the graph to convert $8$ AUD to GBP.
(b) Use the graph to convert $3$ GBP to AUD.
(c) Use $P$ and $Q$ to find the gradient. State its meaning and write $p=kd$, leaving $k$ as a fraction.
(d) Use your equation to convert $45$ AUD to GBP.
(e) Use your equation to find the AUD needed to buy $20$ GBP. Round to $2$ decimal places.

workedExamples.solution_text:
(a) Trace up from $8$ AUD to the line, then across to the GBP axis: $8$ AUD buys $4.8$ GBP.

(b) Trace across from $3$ GBP to the line, then down to the AUD axis: $3$ GBP buys $5$ AUD.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.5cm,y=0.75cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{conversionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{traceRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{traceGreen}{HTML}{4F9B63}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[step=1,gridGrey,very thin] (0,0) grid (10,6);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(10.7,0) node[right] {$d$ (AUD)};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,6.7) node[above] {$p$ (GBP)};
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8,10}{\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.08);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {1,2,3,4,5,6}{\draw[black] (0,\y)--(-0.12,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\y) {$\y$};}
\draw[thick,conversionBlue] (0,0)--(10,6);
\draw[dashed,traceRed,->] (8,0)--(8,4.8);
\draw[dashed,traceRed,->] (8,4.8)--(0,4.8);
\node[left,text=traceRed,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,4.8) {$4.8$};
\draw[densely dotted,traceGreen,->] (0,3)--(5,3);
\draw[densely dotted,traceGreen,->] (5,3)--(5,0);
\node[below,text=traceGreen,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (5,0) {$5$};
\fill[black] (5,3) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (5,3) {$P(5,3)$};
\fill[black] (10,6) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (10,6) {$Q(10,6)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(c) $\begin{align*}k&=\frac{\text{rise}}{\text{run}}\\&=\frac{6-3}{10-5}\\&=\frac35\end{align*}$

The gradient is $\frac35$ GBP per AUD. The line passes through the origin, so $p=\frac35d$.

(d) $\begin{align*}p&=\frac35(45)\\p&=27\end{align*}$

$\$45$ AUD buys $\pounds27$ GBP.

(e) $\begin{align*}20&=\frac35d\\d&=20\div\frac35\\d&=\frac{100}{3}\\d&\approx33.33\end{align*}$

You need $\$33.33$ AUD.

