workedExamples.solution_text:
(a) Trace across from $25$ litres to the line, then down to the gallons axis: approximately $5.6$ gallons. Line thickness and tracing accuracy limit the precision of the reading.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.45cm,y=0.09cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{conversionBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{traceRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{gridGrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\foreach \x in {0,2,4,6,8,10,12}{\draw[gridGrey,very thin] (\x,0)--(\x,60);}
\foreach \y in {0,10,20,30,40,50,60}{\draw[gridGrey,very thin] (0,\y)--(12,\y);}
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(13,0) node[right] {$G$ (gal)};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,66) node[above] {$L$ (litres)};
\node[below left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8,10,12}{\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-1);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {10,20,30,40,50,60}{\draw[black] (0,\y)--(-0.15,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\y) {$\y$};}
\draw[thick,conversionBlue] (0,0)--(12,54);
\fill[black] (8,36) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (8,36) {$(8,36)$};
\draw[dashed,traceRed,->] (0,25)--(5.555556,25);
\draw[dashed,traceRed,->] (5.555556,25)--(5.555556,0);
\node[left,text=traceRed,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,25) {$25$};
\node[below,text=traceRed,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (5.555556,-3) {$\approx5.6$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(b) $\begin{align*}k&=\frac{36}{8}\\k&=4.5\end{align*}$

The conversion factor is $4.5$ litres per gallon, so $L=4.5G$.

(c) $\begin{align*}25&=4.5G\\G&=\frac{25}{4.5}\\G&=\frac{50}{9}\end{align*}$

The exact value within this model is $\frac{50}{9}$ gallons.

